      "commitMessage": "Implement complete API routes for billing, subscriptions, and AP2 payments\n\n## API Routes Implementation\n\n### Billing Routes (/api/billing)\n- GET /tiers - List all subscription tiers\n- GET /tiers/{tier} - Get specific tier info\n- GET /subscription - Get user's subscription status\n- POST /subscription - Create new subscription\n- PUT /subscription/{id}/upgrade - Upgrade tier\n- DELETE /subscription/{id} - Cancel subscription\n- POST /subscription/{id}/reactivate - Reactivate subscription\n- POST /usage/track - Track billable usage\n- GET /usage/monthly - Get monthly usage stats\n- GET /usage/check-limit/{type} - Check if limit exceeded\n\n### AP2 Payment Routes (/api/ap2)\n- POST /complete-flow - Complete full AP2 flow in one call\n- POST /intent-mandate - Create intent mandate\n- POST /cart-mandate - Create cart mandate\n- POST /payment-mandate - Create payment mandate\n- POST /execute-payment - Execute payment via Stripe\n- GET /mandate/{id}/status - Get mandate status\n- GET /user/mandates - List user's mandates\n- GET /stats - Get AP2 usage statistics\n\n### Webhook Routes (/webhooks)\n- POST /stripe - Handle Stripe webhook events\n- GET /health - Webhook health check\n\n## Database\n\n### Migrations\n- Fixed metadata field naming conflict (renamed to extra_data)\n- Successfully migrated all subscription and billing tables\n- Tested on SQLite (development)\n\n## Configuration\n\n### Environment Variables (.env.example)\n- Added complete Stripe configuration\n- Added subscription billing settings\n- Added usage fee configuration\n- Documented all required variables\n\n## Scripts\n\n### Stripe Setup (backend/scripts/setup_stripe.py)\n- Automated Stripe product creation\n- Creates all 3 subscription tiers\n- Generates Price IDs for .env\n- Provides step-by-step instructions\n- Includes testing tips\n\n## Documentation\n\n### API Documentation (API_DOCUMENTATION.md)\n- Complete API reference for all endpoints\n- Request/response examples\n- Authentication guide\n- Error codes and rate limiting\n- Stripe test card numbers\n- Usage examples\n\n## Integration\n\n### Main API (backend/src/api.py)\n- Imported and registered all new routers\n- Billing routes active\n- AP2 payment routes active\n- Webhook routes active\n\n## Features\n\n### Subscription Management\n✅ Multi-tier subscription system\n✅ Trial period support\n✅ Upgrade/downgrade functionality\n✅ Cancellation (immediate or at period end)\n✅ Reactivation support\n\n### Usage Tracking\n✅ Track all billable events\n✅ Automatic overage calculation\n✅ Monthly usage reports\n✅ Limit checking per usage type\n✅ Supports: expenses, AI categorization, OCR scans, AP2 transactions\n\n### AP2 Protocol\n✅ Complete 3-step mandate flow\n✅ Cryptographic signatures\n✅ Constraint validation\n✅ Audit trail generation\n✅ Stripe payment integration\n✅ Simplified one-call flow option\n\n### Webhooks\n✅ Stripe webhook verification\n✅ Automatic subscription sync\n✅ Payment status updates\n✅ Invoice handling\n\n## Testing\n\nReady for testing:\n- Database migrations ✅\n- API routes created ✅\n- Stripe integration ready ✅\n- Webhook handlers ready ✅\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Set up Stripe account\n2. Run setup_stripe.py script\n3. Add Stripe keys to .env\n4. Test API endpoints\n5. Build frontend integration\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e"
     },
